     "design": {
      "purpose": "Draw the image of a figure after a translation, reflection, rotation or dilation, and give its coordinates.",
      "principles": [
       "PRINCIPLE_SYSTEMATIC_VARIATION"
      ],
      "rationale": "Students move each vertex on the grid and join the new points, which is how the move is done by hand before any rule is used. The moves vary from item to item, and the image never overlaps the figure, so each one is seen whole. Writing the coordinates of A′ links the drawing to the coordinate rule for that move.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Rotating 90° by swapping x and y without changing a sign.",
       "Reflecting across the x-axis by changing the sign of x.",
       "Moving the figure the right distance in the wrong direction."
      ]
     },
